          "\"out\" roughly represents style and aesthetic of the image, its best to put it towards the model you want the look of\n\n\"middle\" roughly effects how your prompt effects the image, i suppose its best to aim it towards the model that gets you what you want, for example, i found that when i was combining 2 models, and i put \"anal sex\" as something in my prompt, pointing it more towards one model gave me more consistent anal, while the other gave me less anal, but both options kept the same style, which leads me to believe \"middle\" was taking the \"anal\" prompting aspect into account consideration among other things. i recommend favoring whichever model gets you better prompt following, or whatever model you find you like the prompting of more\n\n\"input\" is currently a wildcard, im unsure what it does, but it could have something to do with smaller details. so for example, if your merging an anime model with a high detail model, you want those small details, pount it more towards the detailed model"
